    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d516">

                <pb facs="0966" n="842" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg842"/>

                <head>No. 512.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hitt
                        to Señor de Zamacona.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-08-16"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 16,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Adverting to your complaint of the 25th of
                    July last, relative to the crossing into Mexico of a sheriff and party, and the
                    capturing of a fugitive criminal who was brought back into this country, I have
                    now the honor to inform you that the Acting Secretary of the Interior has
                    advised this Department, under date of the 9th instant, that the governor of
                    Arizona Territory had been instructed to investigate the subject, and to take
                    all proper measures for the punishment of any guilty persons, and for
                    preservation of peace along the frontier.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>R. R. HITT,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
